The  system  call suspends the calling process until at least one
of the specified asynchronous I/O requests have completed, a sig‐
nal is delivered, or the has passed.  The argument is an array of
pointers to asynchronous I/O requests.  Array members  containing
NULL will be silently ignored.  If is a non‐nil pointer, it spec‐
ifies  a  maximum  interval to suspend.  If is a nil pointer, the
suspend blocks indefinitely.  To effect a poll, the should  point
to a zero‐value timespec structure.  If one or more of the speci‐
fied asynchronous I/O requests have completed, returns 0.  Other‐
wise, it returns ‐1 and sets to indicate the error, as enumerated
below.   The  system call will fail if: The expired before any of
the listed I/O requests completed.  The suspend  was  interrupted
by  a  signal.   The argument contains more than asynchronous I/O
requests, or at least one of the requests is not valid.  The sys‐
tem call is expected to conform to the standard.  The system call
